doc:Factsabs1 rdfs:label "The study proposes an intelligent information system for power grid fault analysis using improved computer communication technology, distributed computing, real-time data transmission, cloud computing, big data analytics, Transformer self-attention, graph neural networks, and edge computing. The system achieves 99.2 percent fault identification and location accuracy, 85 milliseconds average response time, and 1.1 percent average fault prediction error rate." .
